speechtext:
Mr. C. H. CAHAN (St. Lawrence-St.
George) moved for:
1.	A copy of the royal commission and instructions, if any, issued by His Majesty the King to Honourable Vincent Massey as Minister Plenipotentiary to represent the interests of Canada in the United States;
2.	A copy of each and every order in council passed by His Majesty the King in Council or by the Privy Council of Canada, requesting, authorizing or approving of the said appointment of the Honourable Vincent Massey as such Minister Plenipotentiary;
3.	A copy of all correspondence between the Prime Minister of Canada or any minister of the government of Canada, with the Prime Minister of Great Britain or any minister or department of the government of Great Britain relating to the said appointment of the Honourable Vincent Massey as such Minister Plenipotentiary;
4.	A copy of any instructions issued by the government of Canada to the said Minister Plenipotentiary.

Mr. C. II. CAHAN (St. Lawrence-St. George) moved for:
1.	A copy of the royal commission and instructions issued by His Majesty the King to His Excellency Lord Willingdon, as Governor General of Canada;
2.	A copy of each and every order in council passed by His Majesty in Council or by the Privy Council of Canada requesting, authorizing or approving the said appointment of His Excellency Lord Willingdon as Governor General of Canada and the issue of said commission and said instructions.
